  "description": "Kentucky's 3rd Congressional District, which includes much of the Louisville metro area and Jefferson County, is holding a general election on November 3, 2026. Incumbent Democrat Morgan McGarvey, first elected in 2022, is seeking re-election against Republican nominee Maria Teresa Rodriguez, a trauma nurse and small business owner who won a four-way Republican primary on May 19, 2026. The Cook Political Report rates this race as Solidly Democratic. The contest presents voters with a choice between McGarvey's record on organized labor, public education, and reproductive rights, and Rodriguez's platform emphasizing conservative fiscal policy, legal immigration, and public safety.",
